// FL edition of the ship-avoidance site E and the snapshot bindings (the AP twin is the step-2 part of
// src/proxy/ship_steering_sites.h; the snapshot walk ship_avoidance_walk_core.h, the target adjustment av::resolve and the E
// verdict av::site_e_verdict of ship_avoidance_core.h are shared unchanged). Facts: docs/reverse-engineering/fl/ship-avoidance.md
// sections 1-5 and its "Port (2026-11-03)" section; verifier verification/probe/verify_ship_avoidance_sites_fl.py (which emits the
// window rows below, --emit-windows). Every value is an RVA added to x3m::fl::module_base(), or a field offset.
//
// E, the native warn test 0x057600..0x057ccb: `push ebp; mov ebp,esp; and esp,-16` (6 B, three whole instructions, plain
// replay), continuation 0x057606; A in ECX, B / distance / &out at entry [esp+4/+8/+12], integer EAX (0 = no warn), `ret 0xc`
// (all five returns). Incoming flags dead (the AND rewrites them after PUSH/MOV). Callers 0x057db5 / 0x057dd0 (proximity and
// its order-0x12 refresh) and 0x060581 (the avoid order) test EAX at once and read nothing through &out on a false return:
// the stub answers a resolved pair with EAX = 0 and `ret 0xc`, every other register and the flags as they entered.
// Snapshot: [sector+0x50] = the bucket table, heads [table + 0xc class], next [obj], a zero-first-dword sentinel; the station
// part layout of the subtree-radius getter 0x0a39b0 (children +0xc, offsets +0x30.., scale +0x70 under +0x12c & 0x40, radii
// +0xa0/+0xa4); the AP field offsets (ship_avoidance_walk_core.h) hold for FL. The TShips slot is the steering binding
// (ship_steering_sites_fl.h ship_table_slot_rva), passed to the walk through its reader's ship_table().
